      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 1320,
        "height": 1400,
        "content": "# \ud83d\udd0d B2B Research and Scoring Automation\n\nThis workflow automates the entire B2B research process based on a company\u2019s domain. It gathers public data, generates a detailed summary report, and evaluates how well your offer matches the company profile using ISCP (Ideal Service Customer Profile) scoring.\n\n## How it works:\n1. **Input**: Company name and domain via a form or Google Sheet.\n2. **Data Collection**:\n   - Hunter.io: Extracts public email addresses.\n   - Perplexity.ai: Gathers additional company insights from the internet.\n   - LinkedIn (Airtop + Apify): Searches and scrapes LinkedIn company profiles.\n   - Airtop Web Scraper: Extracts data from the company's website.\n3. **Processing**:\n   - All gathered data is merged.\n   - A GPT-based model creates a professional research report.\n   - The ISCP Score is calculated by comparing the report with your offer.\n4. **Output**:\n   - A Google Docs file is created with the report and ISCP match.\n   - You can use this document for lead qualification, outreach, or CRM integration.\n\n## What you need to set up:\n- **API Keys**:\n  - Hunter.io\n  - Perplexity.ai (via HTTP Header)\n  - Airtop (for LinkedIn and Website scraping)\n  - Apify (LinkedIn company data)\n  - OpenAI API (for GPT report and ISCP score)\n  - Google Docs + Google Sheets OAuth (for document generation and optional loop mode)\n\n## Input options:\n- Manual form input (default setup).\n- Optional: Enable reading from Google Sheets and process in a loop.\n\n## Fields to fill in (placeholders to replace):\n\n```plaintext\n[ADD ID OR URL TO DOCS FILE]       \u2192 In the \"Get Offer\" node (Google Docs), set your actual offer document ID or URL.\n[CHOOSE YOUR FOLDER]               \u2192 In the \"Create doc\" node (Google Docs), provide the folder ID where the report will be saved.\n[YOUR APIFY TOKEN]                 \u2192 In both \"Company LinkedIn Account POST\" and \"Company LinkedIn Account GET\" nodes, replace the token in the URL with your Apify API token.\n```\n\nMake sure to replace all placeholders written in square brackets and capital letters.\n"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
  ],
